{"event_type":"review","id":"0a7dffd8985e5113cbd8aec3529ee2cc9d61b315ff26a157f88aa97913134579","occurred_at":"2026-11-12T19:08:23Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/99ee501f2a45ff705de0d506dde8c8e4e28eb7d8a99ca9c4cd4da7f03cad06a9","sha256":"99ee501f2a45ff705de0d506dde8c8e4e28eb7d8a99ca9c4cd4da7f03cad06a9"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b4356a2de89ceb4b65a0765a6a0f7fda6f3df7b095730dcbd30e21433c288179","sha256":"b4356a2de89ceb4b65a0765a6a0f7fda6f3df7b095730dcbd30e21433c288179"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/66d3629d1bf8f5090fea6058e23b66c26e9cc4c78850e46630dd6413e42673f0","sha256":"66d3629d1bf8f5090fea6058e23b66c26e9cc4c78850e46630dd6413e42673f0"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/734a4d03c07785305790008c21802594b31159426a9ead7a0b6c8a160e16c60d","sha256":"734a4d03c07785305790008c21802594b31159426a9ead7a0b6c8a160e16c60d"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/11b9dc67d2c682bc60eeb08bb08fbe61df4182dc7795670d42ab30b409e84f17","sha256":"11b9dc67d2c682bc60eeb08bb08fbe61df4182dc7795670d42ab30b409e84f17"}],"attempt_id":"434cdf0a78f96988b79735c61d811805f356cb393b14484660a857ddabb0f8a5:0:1","base":"b3d45c2625fbd7ca93f43d34c3321291b66d2d6d","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"1dd23e92f5101e95866e54f2e410dc4111e03057","body":"**Make the `platform-time-error` expectation host-independent.**\n\n`now=1e18` is a float, so `utilization_digest` passes it to `_time`, which calls `dt.datetime.fromtimestamp(value, dt.timezone.utc)` (`apps/crq-python/coverage.py:20`, `:491`). On CPython, a failing `gmtime` call raises `OSError` with the platform errno text. The stored expectation records `[Errno 75] Value too large for defined data type` (`apps/crq-python/fixtures/a1-status/utilization.json:2274`). That text comes from the glibc errno for `EOVERFLOW`.\n\n`_capture` stores `str(exc)` (`apps/crq-python/fixtures/a1-status/emit.py:60`), and `--check` compares the full regenerated text (`emit.py:2308`). On a host where `gmtime` fails with a different errno, the message differs and `--check` reports the fixture as stale. Windows follows a different `gmtime_s` branch that sets errno from the returned error code.\n\nThe file header says no host is recorded and that `--check` holds on every host running CPython >= 3.14.7 (`emit.py:14-16`). It names only `fractional-zero-offset-is-applied` as host-dependent (`emit.py:16-18`). This case is undocumented as host-dependent.\n\nEither record only the exception type for this case, or document it in the header as a second host-dependent case.","id":"ca6d875e519f2a2a86762d04f58cc0b76948756310be5983c5390cda97c51217","intervals":[[1480,1480]],"path":"apps/crq-python/fixtures/a1-status/emit.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Make the `platform-time-error` expectation host-independent."}],"head":"115b234dff5446a89918367a33a66d42a5db8cb2","head_tree":"12e1095fbecea104e28eb07c86b1760f1f72bd77","input_scope":[{"blob":"1dd23e92f5101e95866e54f2e410dc4111e03057","intervals":[[1,2315]],"path":"apps/crq-python/fixtures/a1-status/emit.py"},{"blob":"a088f82254db6f282ee7da353c411bfbba355cf1","intervals":[[1,3106]],"path":"apps/crq-python/fixtures/a1-status/merged-current.json"},{"blob":"14b233a8d171f01da38d2f7176d9f87a76affe71","intervals":[[1,608]],"path":"apps/crq-python/fixtures/a1-status/passthrough-receipt.json"}],"job_id":"434cdf0a78f96988b79735c61d811805f356cb393b14484660a857ddabb0f8a5:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"1dd23e92f5101e95866e54f2e410dc4111e03057","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/fixtures/a1-status/emit.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseli